Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: order NPU TX data before ownership publication

The NPU host-ring consumer polls DONE before reading the DMA address and
TXWI. It does not wait for the subsequent CPU-index doorbell. Coherent
allocation does not order these stores, so the barrier in the later queue
kick cannot protect the earlier ownership publication.

Order the copied TXWI and address before publishing DONE, as for RX refill.
Keep descriptor contents, ring accounting and queue metadata unchanged.

Index: mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287/npu.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287.orig/npu.c
+++ mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287/npu.c
@@ -236,9 +236,12 @@ int mt76_npu_dma_add_buf(struct mt76_phy
 	/* TODO: Take into account unlinear skbs */
 	memcpy(desc[q->head].txwi, txwi_ptr, txwi_len);
 	desc[q->head].addr = buf->addr;
-	desc[q->head].ctrl = FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_VEND_LEN_MASK, txwi_len) |
-			     FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, skb->len) |
-			     NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK;
+	/* The NPU polls DONE without waiting for the CPU-index update. */
+	dma_wmb();
+	WRITE_ONCE(desc[q->head].ctrl,
+		   FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_VEND_LEN_MASK, txwi_len) |
+		   FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, skb->len) |
+		   NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK);
 
 	ret = q->head;
 	q->entry[q->head].skip_buf0 = true;
